{"author":"schacon+claude-opus@gmail.com","body":"FULLY PASSING 42/42. Final fix (3b7493a4b): t40 root cause was auto-maintenance, not the merge strategy. After every commit grit runs 'maintenance run --auto'; its commit-graph task counts commits-not-in-graph against maintenance.commit-graph.auto (100), but graph_oids() only read the single info/commit-graph file and ignored the split chain, so a split-chain repo counted ALL commits. Once mixed-merge-gdat crossed 111 commits during setup, a spurious split write collapsed its chain to a bad [8,103] state, yielding num_commits=8 instead of 47. Fixed graph_oids to load CommitGraphChain (covers single + chain). Prior commits this run: 22be7c1d2 (atomic temp+rename writes so hardlinked clone source not corrupted -> recovered 15/16/17/27, root of the 29-vs-39 discrepancy), 33e399c05 (--object-dir global so accepted after subcommand -> t25), e45794473 (try_load_across: split chains across an alternate object dir -> t13/t14; also wired into log.rs validation). Verified no regressions: t6500-gc 35/35, t7900-maintenance 71/72 (unchanged; 1 pre-existing geometric-repack failure, not cg-related). Files: grit/src/commands/commit_graph.rs, grit-lib/src/commit_graph_file.rs, grit/src/commands/log.rs, grit/src/commands/maintenance.rs."}